Subject: [PATCH] Publish content-store views after releasing the store locks

Base: facebook/buck2 9a1876786f32806f6b65fc51f4c1c3077efc38a5 plus the
preceding Sekka patches.

Every store access held the process mutex and the cross-process lock
while it cloned each view, re-hashed it to verify the snapshot, synced
it and renamed it. Five worktrees materializing inputs at once took
turns: summed input materialization reached ~700 s per tree against
0.6 s alone.

A view of an existing canonical object now needs only its lookup and
recorded access under the locks. It is cloned from the open object (whose
descriptor keeps its extents if a peer evicts it), verified, synced and
renamed afterwards, and parent directories are synced before success is
reported. Nothing is renamed unless every snapshot verified. A failed
publication removes its group's view hints and any object that no longer
verifies, under the locks, as the rolled-back transaction did. At most
one group of deferred views holds descriptors at a time. New objects keep
the fully locked path. Staging slots are cleared before the first
canonical stage of a quantum instead of on every access, so lookups skip
that directory sync.

